🚽 Test case: legacy_string() is a legacy/untyped export (STDROT_ANY)
🚽 whose actual runtime result is STDROT_STRING. Its static type is NONE
🚽 (genuinely unknown), so semantic_check_native_call()'s argument check
🚽 for bet's fixed STDROT_BOOL parameter fails open entirely -- there is
🚽 no static way to catch this call passing a string where bet expects a
🚽 bool. enforce_arg_type() (stdrot.c) must catch it at the runtime ABI
🚽 boundary instead, after coerce_arg_to_param()'s attempted conversion
🚽 fails, rather than handing bet's native wrapper a StdrotValue tagged
🚽 something other than what its own StdrotParam declared.
skibidi main {
    bet(legacy_string());
    bussin 0;
}
